HMIS hosts the OPD module for managing outpatient services, used by doctors to register patients, document consultations, order tests, and prescribe treatments, improving efficiency and quality of care.
Outpatient Department (OPD) module is part of the Health Management Information System (HMIS), managing outpatient services and improving efficiency and quality of care in healthcare facilities.
The Health Management Information System (HMIS) hosts the Outpatient Department (OPD) module for managing outpatient services, improving efficiency and quality of care. The OPD module includes features such as a search function for doctors to find patients, a print button for prescriptions, and integration with the pharmacy department for ordering drugs and viewing stock levels. Patients must initially register at a designated registration counter. Doctors use the OPD Doctor Desk interface to manage patients, and patients can book appointments via a mobile app.
Pharmacy A department is integrated with the OPD module, allowing doctors to order drugs and view stock levels, and interacts with other entities.
Search Function Tool enables doctors to search patients by various criteria within the current department list.
Laboratories receive diagnostic test orders from the OPD module and return test results.
Search Function Tool enables doctors to search patients by various criteria within the current department list.
Inventory Integration enables doctors to order drugs and view stock levels from the OPD desk, interacting with the Pharmacy department to facilitate drug ordering and stock management.
Doctors use the OPD Doctor Desk to manage patients, register new ones, and order prescriptions, with features like search functionality and a print button for completed prescriptions, improving efficiency and patient care.
Doctors use the Outpatient Department (OPD) module on the HMIS website to manage outpatient services, register patients, document consultations, order tests, and prescribe treatments, improving efficiency and quality of care.
Total registered patients and their mobile numbers are tracked in real-time in the Department/Unit.
Total registered patients, patient mobile numbers, and doctors are related through various interactions such as contributing to, having, approving, accepting, and allowing switching, with features like real-time data tracking and registration stamping.
A search function tool for doctors to find patients within the current department list using various criteria, enabling search for specific referral patients.
Patients receive medical care and can be registered, searched, or accepted through the OPD system, with their attendance status tracked, and become attended patients after being attended to.
Patients receiving medical care can be registered and sorted by column headers using up and down arrow icons, with sortable columns.
Doctors use the OPD Doctor Desk to manage patients, register new ones, and document consultations. The system allows searching for patients by various criteria and displays a print button for prescriptions once completed. New patients must visit the registration counter for initial registration.
Doctors manage patients and registrations using the OPD system, record vitals and diagnosis, and generate prescriptions. Patients receive outpatient care through the OPD module. The system includes features like search functionality and a print button for prescriptions.
Referral patients are accepted by doctors before being added to the attendance list, with a search function available to find specific patients, and involves acceptance mechanism and source of referrals.
The OPD Doctor Desk is a component of HMIS that enables doctors to manage clinical and administrative tasks. It includes a search function to find patients, a vitals button to record patient vitals, and a print button to preview and print prescriptions for completed patients. The registration counter is where new patients register, using a PPO number as an identifier. The system improves efficiency, enhances patient care, reduces errors, and increases patient satisfaction.
Patient's full name as displayed in the patient list.
Doctor A uses the OPD Doctor Desk to attend to patients, who are registered at the registration counter, and can be searched or accepted through the OPD system, with new registrations requiring a visit to the counter, and existing patients can be registered through the system, which is also available for emergency visits.
Mobile Number is the patient's contact number listed in the system.
OPD Doctor Desk is a component of HMIS OPD module that enables doctors to manage clinical and administrative tasks, register patients, document consultations, order tests, and prescribe treatments, with features like search function, vitals button, and print button for completed prescriptions, improving efficiency and patient care.
The OPD Doctor Desk is a system interface used by doctors to manage patients, register new patients, document consultations, order tests, and prescribe treatments, featuring a search function, customizable patient list view, and a print button for completed prescriptions, ultimately improving efficiency, enhancing patient care, and reducing errors.
A doctor uses the OPD Doctor Desk to manage patients, record vitals and complaints, diagnose, and generate prescriptions. The OPD list displays patients registered or booked for appointments. Patients can be registered, searched, or accepted through the system. The Print Button allows doctors to preview and print prescriptions for completed patients.
Patient's gender is categorized as male, female, or children and is classified into different categories for system classification.
CR number is a unique identifier for registered patients in the hospital system, used for registration and search purposes and is used to identify patients.
Patient information includes full name and category for classification.
Patient information includes full name and age as displayed in the patient list.
Department/unit A is a medical division within a hospital where doctors provide services, register patients, and track attendance status in real-time, available for both existing patient registration and emergency visits.